    {
      "id": 28,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How this dashboard works",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 93,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Sources:** AbuseIPDB (blacklist + per-IP check), AlienVault OTX (threat pulses), CIRCL OSINT MISP feed (threat events), Shodan InternetDB (open ports, CVEs). The collector refreshes them automatically every 6 hours.\n\n**Risk score (0-100)** = **35%** AbuseIPDB confidence + **25%** report volume (log-scaled, 1000+ reports = full) + **20%** threat-intel sightings (OTX + CIRCL, 5+ = full) + **20%** exposure (open ports and known CVEs from Shodan).\n**Levels:** Critical >= 75, High >= 50, Medium >= 25, Low < 25.\n\nClick any IP to open it in AbuseIPDB, or any CVE to open it in the NIST NVD. Use the **Country** filter at the top to focus on one or more countries."
      }
    }
